WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.820
I'm on top of a hill, and like six thousand other hills and high places across the United Kingdom,

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:11.300
this one has one of these on top of it. A short squat pillar, made of concrete, about three feet high.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:16.980
Now why would someone go to the trouble of building six thousand odd 'trig points' as they're known,

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:22.580
trigonometric stations, on high points, because getting there is incredibly difficult, you have to lug tools,

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:25.540
you have to lug the concrete, and you're building something, by the look of it,

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:28.640
that's gonna last for centuries, why would you do that?

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:35.880
Well the answer is mapping. In 1936, and continuing for a quarter of a century, Brigadier Martin Hotine,

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:42.880
and thousands of people, who worked for the Ordnance Survey, built these pillars, in an attempt to retriangulate

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:47.680
Great Britain, and produce the first truly accurate map of the country.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:53.160
See, distance is incredibly hard to measure but angles, angles, you can do precisely.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:58.660
On top of here, you've got some hooks, on which you can set down a 'theodolite', something to measure angles.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:04.060
And then, you build these on hills, so that no matter where you are, if you're at a trig point,

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:09.640
you can see at least two other trig points. And if you can do that, and you know High School trigonometry,

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:14.940
Then you can take one precise baseline measurement across a heath somewhere, the angles you've measured,

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:18.720
and work out the distance across the entire United Kingdom.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:23.800
Nowadays, GPS has taken over of course, they're little more than a landmark for hill-walkers,

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:28.880
but nevertheless, these trig points meant that we had a precise map of the United Kingdom,

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:32.640
with nothing more than a lot of angles, and a lot of maths.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:35.440
